10
00:48:34,285 --> 00:48:40,285
Two-Lane Blacktop is a 1971 American road film directed and edited by Monte
Hellman, from a screenplay by Rudy Wurlitzer and Will Corry.

11
00:53:25,714 --> 00:53:31,714
It stars musicians James Taylor and Dennis Wilson, Warren
Oates, and Laurie Bird in the leading roles.

12
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
The sparse, existentialist plot follows a group of street racers during
a cross-country race through the American Southwest.

13
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
Universal Pictures commissioned the film in the wake
of Easy Rider's monumental success.

14
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Hellman, who had previously worked in low-budget and independent films, developed the screenplay with
Wurlitzer, then-known mainly as an underground writer, during an actual cross-country road trip.

15
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
Filming took place in locations around the
Southwest between August and October 1970.

16
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
On initial release, the film received generally positive
reviews, but was not a commercial success.

17
01:22:34,285 --> 01:22:40,285
Over the years, it developed the reputation of a sleeper hit and a cult classic, and
has been reevaluated as a major work of the New Hollywood movement.

18
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
In 2012, the US Library of Congress selected the film for preservation in the United States
National Film Registry as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant."

19
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
The film explores themes of car race, car mechanic,
chevrolet, road movie, drag race.

